---
import LegalLayout from '../components/LegalLayout.astro';

const COMPANY = 'Luminate Energy LLC';
const SUPPORT_EMAIL = 'adamsuchy@luminate.solar';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — 365"
  description="How 365, operated by Luminate Energy LLC, collects, uses, and protects information."
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  eyebrowNumber="01"
  heading="Privacy"
  headingAccent="policy."
  lastUpdated="May 22, 2026"
>
  <p>
    {COMPANY} (&ldquo;365,&rdquo; &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us&rdquo;) provides the 365
    mobile and web application for solar sales, installation, and operations teams.
    This policy describes what information we collect through 365, how we use it, and
    the choices you have. It is written to align with the categories used in
    Apple&rsquo;s App Privacy questionnaire so that disclosures across the App Store,
    Google Play, and this page stay consistent.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Contact Info</h2>
  <p>
    When you sign in we collect your <strong>email address</strong> and
    <strong> name</strong> from your identity provider (Google or Apple). If you sign
    in with Apple and choose to hide your email, we receive only the private relay
    address Apple generates for you.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Identifiers</h2>
  <p>
    We assign each account a user ID and store your <strong>role</strong> (sales rep,
    crew lead, operations officer, dealer, financier, admin) and your
    <strong> organization or installer affiliation</strong>. These are required to
    scope what records you can see inside the app.
  </p>

  <h2>3. User Content</h2>
  <p>
    Crew leads, installers, and operations users may upload
    <strong> installation photos, signed documents, and job notes</strong>. These are
    stored in our Supabase Storage <code>uploads</code> bucket and are visible only to
    other authenticated users at the same organization who have permission to view the
    associated job.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Usage Data &amp; Diagnostics</h2>
  <p>
    We log basic application events (page views, sign-in success/failure, errors) so
    we can debug the app and improve it. These logs are not sold or shared with
    advertisers.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Push Notification Tokens</h2>
  <p>
    If you enable notifications, we store the push token issued to your device by:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Apple Push Notification service (APNs) on iOS,</li>
    <li>Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) on Android, and</li>
    <li>Web Push (VAPID) in browsers.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Tokens are used solely to deliver in-app notifications (new leads, job updates,
    commission events). You can revoke notifications at any time in your device
    settings, and the token will be removed from our records on next sign-in.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Location (Future Feature)</h2>
  <p>
    A future version of 365 will support <strong>optional background location</strong>
    for crew leads on active installation routes (drive-time tracking, on-site
    check-in). This feature is not enabled in the current release. When it ships, it
    will be opt-in, will display the standard iOS &ldquo;Always Allow&rdquo; prompt
    with a clear purpose string, and will only collect location while a job is active.
    We disclose it here in advance to set accurate expectations.
  </p>

  <h2>7. How We Use Your Data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Authenticate you and route you to the correct dashboard for your role.</li>
    <li>Display jobs, commissions, leads, and team information for your organization.</li>
    <li>Send notifications you have opted into.</li>
    <li>Diagnose errors and improve the app.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal data, share it with advertisers, or
    use it for ad targeting.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Service Providers</h2>
  <p>
    We rely on the following third parties as processors. Each is bound by their own
    privacy commitments:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> &mdash; authentication, database, file storage.</li>
    <li><strong>Vercel</strong> &mdash; web hosting.</li>
    <li><strong>Google &amp; Apple</strong> &mdash; sign-in providers.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> &mdash; transactional email (invites).</li>
    <li><strong>Apple APNs, Google FCM, Web Push</strong> &mdash; notification delivery.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. Data Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep account data for as long as your account is active. If you request account
    deletion (see Section 11) we remove your profile, uploaded content, and push
    tokens within 30 days, subject to any records we are required to retain for
    commission, tax, or legal purposes.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>
    365 is a workforce app intended for users 18 years or older. We do not knowingly
    collect data from anyone under 13.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Your Rights &amp; Account Deletion</h2>
  <p>
    You can request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal data by
    emailing <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
    Users in California, the EEA, or the UK have additional rights under CCPA / GDPR;
    we honor those requests on the same channel.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the app evolves. The &ldquo;Effective&rdquo; date at
    the top reflects the most recent revision. Material changes will be announced
    inside the app.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {COMPANY}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
